# docportal starts up: main.startup runs these steps in order, and main hands
# the address and the portal to the HTTP server.
# By hand: dfd --box 300x150 --per-row 5 --number docs/flow.dfd -o flow.svg

{Operator}
> arguments, environment
[1. Read the configuration
 from the flags and the environment
 (main.parseConfig)]
> specs directory name, spec path
[2. Open the specs directory and pair it with the spec path
 so that the portal cannot read outside the directory
 (main.openSpecs)]
    > specs directory name
    < specs directory handle
    <Specs directory>
> portal configuration, content directory name
[4. Open the named content directory, if any, and add it to the portal configuration
 so that the portal cannot read outside the content directory
 (main.openDocs)]
    > content directory name
    < content directory handle
    <Content directory>
> portal configuration, Try It setting
[5. Add the Try It setting to the portal configuration
 so that the viewer page shows or hides the Try It console
 (main.setTryIt)]
> portal configuration
[3. Build the portal
 or refuse a spec path outside the specs directory or missing Elements assets
 (portal.New)]
> address, portal
{HTTP server}

# type: arguments = []string
# type: environment = func(string) string
# type: specs directory name = string
# type: spec path = string
# type: content directory name = string
# type: Try It setting = bool
# type: portal configuration = portal.Config
# type: address = string
# type: portal = net/http.Handler
